    80	## 7. Validation ladder, controls, parity gate, acceptance
    81	
    82	Static checks → new tests + `verify_exp03_pins` against `ckpt/yaw_rotation/binding_report.json` (live sha256 of the 12 pinned files == their reviewed blobs at `62c9107b…`; `tests/test_exp03_record_tools.py` alone only exercises the validators on synthetic records) + the exp_04/exp_07 record suites → smoke (`--batches 0`, CPU) → **probe** on GPU 1: `released_k8` on the 17 room-spanning canonical batches (272 queries; identical batch composition to the full run, so its per-sample values are a subset of the full run's) at all five angles, with timing of inference / inversion / metrics / writing separately and a thread budget of 16 torch threads, one process; **controls** on the same probe: `ctrl_full_turn` (k = 512; identity path through `rotate_scene_yaw`, plumbing only), `ctrl_zero_repeat` (fresh k = 0 inference under its own id), `ctrl_k128_repeat` (fresh nonzero repeat) — all three must match their originals to 1e-6 (waveforms, log-spec) and 1e-9 (acoustic metrics). **Parity gate vs exp_03** (`sweep_released/per_sample_yaw.json`, same GPU class, TF32 off, same manifest / gl_seed / batch shape) on the probe queries, per angle in {0, 64, 128, 256, 384}: (a) per-sample `logspec_mad` |Δ| ≤ 1e-5 for every query; (b) per-sample `edt_err` / `c50_err` / `t60_err` |Δ| ≤ 1e-4 s / 1e-3 dB / 0.01 % for ≥ 99.5 % of queries (Griffin-Lim can amplify float noise for a few); (c) the **paired Δ on the probe queries** from the new run and from exp_03 agree within max(5 % of |Δ_exp03|, 2e-5 s / 2e-4 dB / 2e-3 %) and have the same sign, for every angle and metric. **All three criteria (a), (b), (c) are binding**: if the GPU probe fails any of them the launch is blocked and the cause investigated. If only the CPU fallback is available and fails any criterion, the arm proceeds as a **separate CPU protocol**: Δ, G and R are computed **entirely from that CPU run** (never from exp_03's GPU errors — test 16), exp_03's values appear only in a separately labelled historical-comparison table with the discrepancy tabulated, and no "replication" wording is used. An arm is called an exp_03 replication only after `parity_exp03` passes on the probe **and** on the full results. `control_k8` / `cyl_k8` run the same probe gate against `sweep_control` / `sweep_cyl`; `released_k1` runs the controls only (no predecessor). Each arm's full run is forecast from its own probe timing (K = 1 and K = 8 forward costs differ). **Full-run acceptance:** 6 337 queries in canonical order, every angle present, `meta.complete`, `check_online` passes, EDT/C50 finite counts at k = 0 equal exp_03's for the replicated arms, waveform arrays' sha256s recorded, worklog acceptance entry written before launch.
